translations.text:
Hair once grew here, where now I bare a skull;
a baldness not only clean but noble;
my head has turned into a buttock:
it calls for breeches rather than a hat.


If, Calvin as I am, I were a Luther,
nothing could save me from the fire;
nor bladder nor melon bulges so much
when set beneath the August sun.


Those in Madrid who scratch another's hair
want to convert me to wigs,
plucking all the other skulls.


I always condemn the requiem of a lock;
let their pates wear shells:
let my itch slide over bald thunder.

When your mother bore you cuckolded,
your planet was a horn of the moon;
your cradle was made of hornwood,
and its little turret a very sharp horn.


You often spent horns on your trinkets;
the milk you sucked was goat's milk;
Fortune gave you a horn for arms
and a bull atop your shield.


I see you turned into a pen of horns;
you tread horns with cuckold's feet;
each morning a horn greets you.


All cuckolds have a temple in you.
So, cuckold of yourself, where do you walk
with so horned a star?
